" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135717750.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Amazon has agreed to pay $3 million to eligible Arizona Prime customers who allegedly faced difficulties cancelling their $139 annual memberships. The settlement with Arizona Attorney General Kris Mayes also requires the retail giant to contribute $1.5 million towards consumer protection efforts, pay $1.5 million in legal fees and donate another $1 million to food charities. The company has denied violating any state laws.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/amazon-to-refund-3-million-to-prime-customers-over-six-step-cancellation-process-also-agrees-to-donate-1-million-to-charities-and-allocate-1-5-million-to-consumer-protection/articleshow/135717750.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/amazon-to-refund-3-million-to-prime-customers-over-six-step-cancellation-process-also-agrees-to-donate-1-million-to-charities-and-allocate-1-5-million-to-consumer-protection/articleshow/135717750.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T23:10:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135717931,imgsize-49420.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Washington woman wins five-year protection order against ex-husband]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135714976.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Washington woman applied for a domestic violence protection order after her ex-husband's alarming actions. He allegedly accessed her devices and tracked her credit card spending, despite a no-contact order. Following his violent behavior, the court issued a five-year protection order, which he challenged unsuccessfully. The Washington Court of Appeals confirmed the protection order, citing his continued violations as grounds for its necessity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-woman-says-her-ex-husband-tracked-her-spending-accessed-her-homes-alexa-system-and-repeatedly-stalked-her-despite-a-no-contact-order-an-appeals-court-upheld-a-five-year-domestic-violence-protection-order/articleshow/135714976.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-woman-says-her-ex-husband-tracked-her-spending-accessed-her-homes-alexa-system-and-repeatedly-stalked-her-despite-a-no-contact-order-an-appeals-court-upheld-a-five-year-domestic-violence-protection-order/articleshow/135714976.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T22:58:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135715181,imgsize-67688.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Los Angeles charity raises record $4 million at gala honouring Rob and Michele Reiner’s legacy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135711615.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Children's Institute hosted an extravagant gala in Beverly Hills to honor Rob and Michele Reiner's impactful legacy. Their children, Jake and Romy, presented the prestigious Champion for Change Award to the incredible Jamie Lee Curtis. With over 600 attendees, the event raised an astounding $4 million to support vital programs for children and families throughout Los Angeles County, celebrating the Reiners' lifelong commitment to social advocacy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/months-after-the-deaths-of-rob-and-michele-reiner-a-los-angeles-childrens-charity-raised-a-record-4-million-at-a-gala-honouring-their-legacy-their-children-presented-an-award-to-jamie-lee-curtis/articleshow/135711615.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/months-after-the-deaths-of-rob-and-michele-reiner-a-los-angeles-childrens-charity-raised-a-record-4-million-at-a-gala-honouring-their-legacy-their-children-presented-an-award-to-jamie-lee-curtis/articleshow/135711615.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T20:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135711761,imgsize-87212.cms"/></item></channel></rss>